---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '~/lib/site';
const updated = '2026-04-19';
---

<Base title="Terms" description="Terms of use for Glitch Trade." pageType="WebPage">
  <section class="container-app py-20 max-w-prose-tight">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-subtle text-fluid-sm">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose mt-10 text-muted [&_h2]:text-fg [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_h2]:text-fluid-xl [&_h3]:text-fg [&_h3]:mt-6 [&_h3]:mb-2 [&_h3]:text-fluid-base [&_p]:my-3 [&_strong]:text-fg [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_li]:my-1.5 [&_a]:text-brand">
      <p>
        By accessing {site.domain}, creating an account, or using the Glitch
        Trade bot or any related software, API, or data feed (collectively,
        the "Service") you agree to these Terms of Use. The Service is
        operated by {site.parent} ("we", "us", "our"). Nothing on this site
        or in the bot constitutes a binding offer, a recommendation, or
        professional advice — it is marketing content and software tooling.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Educational &amp; informational use only</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is intended for informational and educational use. All
        signals, model outputs, analyses, dashboards, screenshots, and
        commentary are provided <strong>for general information only</strong>
        and must not be interpreted as a personal recommendation or an
        invitation to transact in any security, commodity, or digital asset.
        If you need advice tailored to your situation, consult a licensed
        professional in your jurisdiction.
      </p>

      <h2>2. No investment advice; no registered status</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Glitch Trade does not provide investment, financial, legal,
        or tax advice.</strong> We are not:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>A registered broker-dealer, investment adviser, or FINRA/SEC-licensed entity in the United States;</li>
        <li>A SEBI-registered Investment Adviser (IA) or Research Analyst (RA) in India under the SEBI (Investment Advisers) Regulations 2013 or SEBI (Research Analysts) Regulations 2014;</li>
        <li>Licensed by the UAE Securities and Commodities Authority (SCA), the Dubai Virtual Assets Regulatory Authority (VARA), the DFSA, or the ADGM Financial Services Regulatory Authority (FSRA);</li>
        <li>Authorised by the UK Financial Conduct Authority (FCA), nor registered with any EU national competent authority under MiCA, MiFID II, or related frameworks.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Signals, model outputs, and commentary are <strong>not tailored to
        your personal financial situation, risk tolerance, or regulatory
        position</strong>. You are solely responsible for every trading
        decision you make.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Past performance &amp; hypothetical results</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Past performance does not guarantee future results.</strong>
        Any historical metrics, backtests, paper-trading runs, or simulated
        results shown on this site or inside the bot are hypothetical. Live
        trading outcomes will differ from simulated ones, often materially.
      </p>
      <h3>3.1 CFTC Rule 4.41-style disclosure</h3>
      <p class="font-mono text-fluid-xs uppercase tracking-wide">
        Hypothetical performance results have many inherent limitations,
        some of which are described below. No representation is being made
        that any account will or is likely to achieve profits or losses
        similar to those shown. In fact, there are frequently sharp
        differences between hypothetical performance results and the actual
        results subsequently achieved by any particular trading program.
        One of the limitations of hypothetical performance results is that
        they are generally prepared with the benefit of hindsight. In
        addition, hypothetical trading does not involve financial risk, and
        no hypothetical trading record can completely account for the impact
        of financial risk in actual trading — for example, the ability to
        withstand losses or adhere to a particular trading program in spite
        of trading losses. There are numerous other factors related to the
        markets in general or to the implementation of any specific trading
        program which cannot be fully accounted for in the preparation of
        hypothetical performance results, and all of which can adversely
        affect actual trading results.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Trading risk</h2>
      <p>
        Trading cryptocurrencies, derivatives, and other financial
        instruments involves a <strong>substantial risk of loss</strong> and
        is not suitable for every investor. You can lose some or all of the
        capital you commit. If you trade on leverage, margin, or
        derivatives, <strong>you may lose more than your initial
        deposit</strong>. Do not trade with money you cannot afford to lose.
        You are responsible for understanding the fee structure, margin
        mechanics, liquidation terms, and funding rates of any exchange you
        connect to Glitch Trade.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Eligibility &amp; jurisdictional restrictions</h2>
      <h3>5.1 Age requirement</h3>
      <p>
        You must be at least 18 years old (or the age of majority in your
        jurisdiction, whichever is higher) to use the Service.
      </p>
      <h3>5.2 User responsibility</h3>
